scope: "The `device_monitor` widget — a container that composes ITSELF at runtime from what a device advertises. It discovers a device's capabilities (temperature, uptime, disk, CPU, power-cycle, …) and stamps the matching component (spec 14) for each. Capability-driven composition: the device's published surface, not the author, decides which widgets appear. Includes the data-source question (Prometheus as aggregator + semantic bridge)."
audience: "ComposeUX renderer + discovery implementers; fleet-ops surface authors; device-adapter authors (what to advertise)"
boundary: "One new container widget (`device_monitor`) + a capability-descriptor extension to ComposeIO discovery + a declarative capability→component map. Builds ON spec 14 (components are the vocabulary) and spec 13 (mcp_action for the control capabilities). Does not change existing static layout — it is an additional, dynamic module type."
not-this: "Not auto-magic that infers widgets from raw values (that is name-sniffing — DM-2 requires ADVERTISED capability metadata); not a bypass of the mcp_action allowlist (DM-7: capability advertisement is not authority); not a Prometheus/Grafana replacement (DM-6: complementary, not competitive); not a metrics store (the bus carries current semantic state, not history)."
